      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"McBehrer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/48/1850_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> McBehrer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>One of mine was on Divine Focus; when I figured out that it worked at the beginning of EVERY turn and not just every FANATIC turn, it made a lot more sense as to why it had the (previously thought to be) RIDICULOUS 4 damage cost on it.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Those words are so easy to miss and yet can completely change the card.</p>\n<p>For instance, I thought Ra's Imbued Fire (I think that's the name) changed <em>everyone's</em> damage type to Fire, not just the heroes.&nbsp; So for a while I was thinking, \"Why would I ever play this card?&nbsp; It gives everyone, villains included a +1 damage buff.&nbsp; Maybe if I wanted the game over faster?\"</p>",
      "post_number": 8,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:09:22.375Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
